A directory argument whose name contains a `-` is walked like any directory, giving a glob view of the one file inside it.
== args
input/dir-special
== file input/dir-special/file.md
---
description: Special dir file.
---
# special
== stdout
glob view: input/dir-special
input/dir-special/file.md (4 lines): description: "Special dir file."
== stderr
== exit 0
